<title>FINLAND: FINNISH BONDS END FIRMER, UNFAZED BY U.S. Q2 GDP.</title>
<headline>FINNISH BONDS END FIRMER, UNFAZED BY U.S. Q2 GDP.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish bonds closed a fair session firmer on Thursday, unshaken by an upward revision in U.S. second-quarter GDP, dealers said.</p>
<p>U.S. Q2 GDP was revised to 4.8 percent from 4.2 percent. Most European bonds slipped after the news.</p>
<p>&quot;We are just so bullish now, it seems nothing is able to disrupt the sentiment, one Helsinki dealer said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom + 358 - 0 - 680 50 240</p>
